    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0333" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg249"/>

                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Colon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of the Navy</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.:</hi></p>
                <p>Receipt of your telegram of November 2 is acknowledged. Prior to receipt this
                    morning about 400 men were landed here by the Government of Colombia from
                    Cartagena. No revolution has been declared on the Isthmus and no disturbances.
                    Railway company have declined to transport these troops except by request of the
                    governor of Panama. Request has not been made. It is possible that movement
                    maybe made to-night at Panama to declare independence, in which event I will * *
                    * (message mutilated here) here. Situation is most critical if revolutionary
                    leaders act.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hubbard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
